{UTF-8}
Data from NonFans=NonFans* Baseline Discussion Per Hour*Average Workhour of Each Fan*\
		gamma*EXP(-s*beta)
	~	comment/Month
	~	Conversation from Non-Fans
		Discouraged Discussion is regular discussion rate by default
		r is 1 by default
	|

Proportion data making=Data from DataMaking/Traffic Data
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

s=0
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

Conversion rate per show exposure=0.05
	~	Dmnl/show [?,?,0.01]
	~	the probability for each show, if watched, to turn a non-fan into a fan
	|

Data from Interpersonal Interaction=(Remaining workforce after data making*(1-Allocation to fan art\
		))*Baseline Discussion Per Hour
	~	comment/Month
	~	discussion not driven by data-making
	|

Traffic Data=(Data from DataMaking*w+Data from Interpersonal Interaction+Data from NonFans\
		)
	~	comment/Month
	~	Traffic Data
		(comment/Month + comment/Month)/(comment/month)
	|

signal=Traffic Data/baseline TD
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

change in perception=(signal-Perceived Business Value)/Time to update PBV
	~	Dmnl/Month
	~		|

Effect of Fan Art=Number of Relavent fan art/Reference Arts
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

Effect of Interaction=Data from Interpersonal Interaction/Reference Discussion
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

NonFans= INTEG (Churn Rate-Recruitment,
		100000)
	~	person
	~		|

Recruitment from show watching=NonFans*Show exposure*Conversion rate per show exposure
	~	person/Month
	~	advertising effectiveness
	|

Erosion time=EXP(-Proportion data making*kappa)*Base erosion time
	~	Month
	~	Maybe other formulation would also work for a decreasing function
	|

Fan Size= INTEG (Recruitment-Churn Rate,
		0)
	~	person
	~		|

Show exposure=Relevant Shows*Show exposure probability
	~	show/Month
	~	One's probability of liking the idol with all the shows exposed; \
		Conversion probability from direct exposure
	|

Churn Rate=Fan Size/Erosion time
	~	person/Month
	~		|

DM Discussion Per Hour=
	Baseline Discussion Per Hour*(1+(maxfactor-1)*beta)
	~	comment/Hour
	~	DM discussion rate
	|

Baseline Discussion Per Hour=
	5
	~	comment/Hour [0,10]
	~		|

Reference Arts=
	300
	~	art [0,10000,100]
	~		|

Reference Discussion=
	50000
	~	comment/Month [0,1e+06,100000]
	~	50000
	|

Data from DataMaking=POWER(Total Workhours Available*alpha/Reference Hours, 1-lambda)\
		*Reference Hours*DM Discussion Per Hour
	~	comment/Month
	~	comments made for data-making
	|

Total Workhours Available=
	Fan Size*Average Workhour of Each Fan
	~	Hour/Month
	~		|

gamma=0.1
	~	Dmnl [0,10]
	~	Appealing to Outsiders
	|

Attractiveness of fan circle=
	(2/(1+EXP(-Effect of Fan Art))-1)*
	(2/(1+EXP(-Effect of Interaction))-1)
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

maxfactor=
	5
	~	Dmnl [1,20]
	~	max speed up factor
	|

Base erosion time=3
	~	Month [0,?]
	~		|

lambda=0
	~	Dmnl [0,0.3]
	~	Motivation Decay Rate
	|

kappa=0.5
	~	Dmnl [0,1]
	~	Cross-Platform Competitive Pressure
	|

Reference Hours=
	1
	~	Hour/Month
	~		|

Ratio of Show to Art=
	10
	~	Dmnl/show [0,100,0.1]
	~		|

New fan art=
	Remaining workforce after data making*Allocation to fan art*Fan art per hour*Relevant Shows\
		*Ratio of Show to Art
	~	art/Month
	~	hour/month*art/hour* show*1/show
	|

conversion rate=
	Attractiveness of fan circle*Effect of ingroup att on WOM
	~	Dmnl/person
	~	rate of converting non-fans into fans through WOM
	|

Show Erosion=
	Relevant Shows/(Show obsolescence time)
	~	show/Month
	~		|

baseline TD=500000
	~	comment/Month [0,500000,100000]
	~		|

Show exposure probability=0.05
	~	Dmnl/(Month) [0,0.2,0.01]
	~	the probability for a relevant show to be watched by a non-fan
	|

New Shows per Month=
	POWER(Perceived Business Value, Effect of PBV on Show)*"reference show/month"
	~	show/Month
	~		|

Show obsolescence time=
	36
	~	Month [0,36,6]
	~		|

Relevant Shows= INTEG (
	New Shows per Month-Show Erosion,
		1)
	~	show
	~		|

Effect of PBV on Show=
	0.5
	~	Dmnl [0,0.5,0.01]
	~		|

Fan art per hour=
	0.0002
	~	art/Hour [0,0.001,1e-05]
	~		|

Allocation to fan art=
	0.5
	~	Dmnl
	~	This allocation is inherent for fans.
	|

w=
	0.9
	~	Dmnl [0,1]
	~	Contribution of Gaming Engagement to Signals
	|

Average Workhour of Each Fan=
	2*30
	~	Hour/person/Month
	~		|

Remaining workforce after data making=
	Total Workhours Available*(1-alpha)
	~	Hour/Month
	~		|

contact rate=
	0.2
	~	person/Month [0,0.5,0.05]
	~	contact rate between fans and non-fans
	|

Recruitment from fans=
	(contact rate*conversion rate*Fan Size*NonFans)/(Fan Size+NonFans)
	~	person/Month
	~	(contact rate*conversion rate*Fan Size*Passerby)/(Fan Size+Passerby)
	|

Time to update PBV=
	12
	~	Month [0,36,1]
	~	Time to adjust business value perception
	|

beta=0.8
	~	Dmnl [0,1,0.1]
	~	Platform Strategy: Intensity of DM Policy
	|

fan art erosion=
	Number of Relavent fan art/ Fan art obsolescence time
	~	art/Month
	~		|

Effect of ingroup att on WOM=
	1
	~	Dmnl/person [0,5,0.1]
	~		|

Perceived Business Value= INTEG (
	change in perception,
		0)
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

Recruitment=
	Recruitment from show watching+Recruitment from fans
	~	person/Month
	~		|

"reference show/month"=
	0.2
	~	show/Month [0,0.5,0.01]
	~	average idol's show per month
	|

alpha=0.8
	~	Dmnl [0,1]
	~	Idol Agency's Strategy: Allocation to data making
	|

Number of Relavent fan art= INTEG (
	New fan art-fan art erosion,
		1)
	~	art [0,?]
	~		|

Fan art obsolescence time=
	36
	~	Month [0,36,6]
	~		|

********************************************************
	.Control
********************************************************~
		Simulation Control Parameters
	|

FINAL TIME  = 36
	~	Month
	~	The final time for the simulation.
	|

INITIAL TIME  = 0
	~	Month
	~	The initial time for the simulation.
	|

SAVEPER  = 
        TIME STEP
	~	Month [0,?]
	~	The frequency with which output is stored.
	|

TIME STEP  = 0.0078125
	~	Month [0,?]
	~	The time step for the simulation.
	|

